1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,500
The Fourth Great
and Bountiful Human Empire.
Every fact beams out from here.

2
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:13,000
That's what I call power. 600
channels coming out of Satellite
Five, broadcasting everywhere.

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,300
This technology's wrong.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,700
Trouble? Oh, yeah.

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:21,400
This is not the Fourth Great
and Bountiful Human Empire.

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,700
Humans are allowed to live here
by kind permission of my client.

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,600
Who controls Satellite Five?

8
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:30,600
The Mighty Jagrafess of the
Holy Hadrojassic Maxarodenfoe.

9
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:33,400
You mean that thing's in
charge of Satellite Five?

10
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,000
Once you go to Floor
500, you never come back.

11
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:47,300
You'll have to stay and explain
it, no-one's gonna believe me.

12
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,300
Oh, they might start
believing a lot of things now.

13
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,500
The human race should accelerate.
All back to normal.

14
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,900
What is it? What's happening?

15
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,600
Oh, my God!

16
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:14,400
I don't believe it, why
did they put you in there?

17
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,400
They never said you were coming!

18
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:17,900
What happened? I was. . .

19
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,800
Careful now, oh. . .

20
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:21,700
Oh, mind yourself!

21
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:25,900
Oh, that's the transmat,
it scrambles your head.
I was sick for days.

22
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,600
You all right?

23
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:31,600
So. . .what's your name,
then, sweetheart?

24
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,000
The Doctor, I think, I was. . .

25
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:35,800
I don't know what happened!

26
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:38,000
You got chosen.

27
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Chosen for what?

28
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,500
You're a housemate! You're in
the house! Isn't that brilliant?

29
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,700
That's not fair, we've got
eviction in five minutes!

30
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,900
I've been here for all nine weeks,
I've followed the rules,

31
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,800
I haven't had a single warning,
and he comes swanning in!

32
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:56,000
If they keep changing the rules,
I'm gonna protest, I am.

33
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,400
I'm gonna paint the walls.

34
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,500
'Would the Doctor please
come to the Diary Room?'

35
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,100
You are live on Channel 44, 000.

36
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:22,400
Please do not swear.
You have GOT to be kidding.

37
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:05,300
Oh. . .

38
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,200
Ah. . .

39
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:10,000
What happened? It's all right.

40
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,800
It's the transmat.

41
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:14,600
It does your head in,
you get a bit of amnesia.

42
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,500
What's your name?

43
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:19,700
Rose. But. . .where's the Doctor?

44
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,800
Just remember,
do what the android says.

45
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:25,000
Don't provoke it.

46
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,300
The android's word is law.

47
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:29,700
What do you mean, android?
Like a robot?

48
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:32,600
Positions, everyone, thank you!

49
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:36,000
Come on, hurry up!
The contestants are in place,

50
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:38,100
the cameras. . . Oh, steady!

51
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,800
I was travelling,

52
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,600
with the Doctor and a
man called Captain Jack?

53
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:47,000
The Doctor wouldn't just leave me.

54
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,800
That's enough chat!

55
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,700
Positions! Final call. Good luck.

56
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:56,100
But I'm not supposed to be here.
It says Rose on the podium.

57
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:58,000
Come on.

58
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:12,600
Hold on. . .

59
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:14,800
I must be going mad.

60
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:21,500
It can't be, this looks like. . .
Android activated!

61
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:24,900
Oh, my God, the android. . .

62
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:28,700
The An. . .droid.

63
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:31,500
Welcome. . .to the Weakest Link!

64
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:37,300
Here we go again.
We've got our work cut out for us.

65
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:40,900
I don't know, he's sort of
handsome. Good lantern jaw.

66
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:43,500
Lantern jaws are so last year.

67
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:46,800
Sorry. . . Nice to meet you,
ladies, but where exactly am I?

68
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:49,400
We're giving you
a brand new image.

69
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,200
Hold on, I was with the Doctor. . .

70
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,100
Why, is there something
wrong with what I'm wearing?

71
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:57,800
It's all very 20th century,
where did you get that denim?

72
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:01,600
A little place in Cardiff,
it was called. . .the Top Shop.

73
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:04,500
Ah, design classic!

74
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,900
We're gonna have to
find you some new colours,

75
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
maybe get rid of that Oklahoma
farm boy thing you've got going.

76
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,600
Just stand still and let the
defabricator work its magic.

77
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,100
What's a defabricator?

78
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:27,100
OK, defabricator. Does
exactly what it says on the tin.

79
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:29,500
Am I naked in front of
millions of viewers?

80
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,100
Absolutely!

81
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:35,600
Ladies. . .your viewing
figures just went up.

82
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:42,200
I can't open it. It's got a deadlock
seal, ever since Big Brother
504 when they all walked out.

83
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,200
You must remember that.
What about this?

84
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:49,600
Oh, that's exoglass, you'd need a
nuclear bomb to get through.
Don't tempt me.

85
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:55,800
I know you're not supposed to
talk about the outside world,
but you must've been watching.

86
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:59,100
Do people like me? Lynda, Lynda
with a Y, not Linda with an I,

87
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:03,100
she got forcibly evicted cos she
damaged a camera. Am I popular?

88
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:06,200
I don't remember.
Oh, but does that mean I'm nothing?

89
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:11,000
Some people get this far
just cos they're insignificant.
Doesn't anybody notice me?

90
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,100
No, you're nice, you're. . .sweet.

91
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:18,900
Everybody thinks you're sweet. Oh,
is that right? Is that what I am?

92
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
No-one's ever told me that before.

93
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:23,400
Am I sweet? Really?

94
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,900
Yeah, dead sweet.

95
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,500
Thank you.

96
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:31,800
It's a wall. Isn't there
supposed to be a garden out there?

97
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:35,200
Don't be daft, no-one's got a
garden any more! Who's got a garden?

98
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:37,100
Don't tell me you've got a garden!

99
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:39,500
No, I've just got the Tardis.

100
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:44,100
I remember.
That's the amnesia! So what
happened, where did they get you?

101
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:48,700
We'd just left
Raxacoricofallapatorius and then we
went to Kyoto, that's right,

102
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:54,000
Japan in 1336, and we only
just escaped. We were together
and we were laughing and then. . .

103
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,600
there was this light,

104
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:59,400
this white light
coming through the walls, and then. . .

105
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,200
I woke up here.

106
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:05,500
Yeah, that's the transmat beam,
that's how they pick the housemates.

107
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:10,000
Oh, Lynda with a Y. . .

108
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,700
Sweet little Lynda.

109
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:15,400
It's worse than that.

110
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:17,800
I'm not just some passing traveller.

111
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:20,900
No stupid little transmat
gets inside my ship.

112
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:26,900
That beam was 15 million
times more powerful, which
means. . .this isn't just a game.

113
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,300
There's something else going on.

114
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,300
Well, here's the latest update
from the Big Brother house.

115
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,200
I'm getting out,

116
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:40,000
I'm gonna find my friends. . .

117
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,800
and then I'm gonna find you.

118
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:52,300
Need a word. Hold on.

119
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:55,900
Let me finish this. 19, 18. . .

120
00:07:55,900 --> 00:08:00,000
17, 16, 15. . .

121
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:03,400
Thank you, people, transmitting in. . .

122
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:07,000
12, 11, 10. . .

123
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:11,100
But I need to find the Doctor.
Just shut up and play the game!

124
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:13,000
All right, then. . .what the hell?

125
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,200
I'm gonna play to win!

126
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,800
And. . .cue.

127
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:20,700
Let's play the Weakest Link!

128
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:26,700
Start the clock. Agorax,
the name of which basic foodstuff
is an anagram of the word "beard"?

129
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,400
Bread. Correct.

130
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:33,900
Fitch, in the Pantraffic Calendar,
which month comes after Hoob?

131
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,800
Is it. . .Clavadoe?

132
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:43,400
No, Pandoff. Rose, in maths,
what is 258 minus 158? 100.

133
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,300
Correct. Rodrick. Bank!

134
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:48,300
Which letter of the alphabet
appears in the word "dangle"

135
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:51,000
but not in the word "gland"?

136
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,900
E. Correct.

137
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:59,700
Colleen, in social security, what

138
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:07,500
Correct. Broff, the Great Cobalt
Pyramid is built on the remains of
which famous old Earth institute?

139
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:11,100
Touchdown. No, Torchwood.

140
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:16,100
Agorax, in language, all five
examples of which type of letter

141
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:19,500
appear in the word facetious?
Vowels.

142
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:24,600
Correct.
Fitch, in biology, which blood
cells contain iron - red or white?

143
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:25,600
Erm. . .

144
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:28,900
White. No, red.

145
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:35,400
Rose, in the holovid
series Jupiter Rising,
the Grexnik is married to whom?

146
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:37,700
How should I know?

147
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:40,500
Why is she laughing?

148
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,900
Rodrick, in maths. . .

149
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:46,800
Oh, my God, I think she knows.

150
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:49,400
And I've got a housemate
who appeared out of nowhere.

151
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,400
I told you.
It's like the game's running itself.

152
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:58,400
It's the buccaneer look - a
little a dash of pirate and just a
tweak of President Schwarzenegger.

153
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:01,600
I'm not sure about the vest, what
about a bit of colour to lift it?

154
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:04,400
Absolutely not,
never wear black with colour.

155
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:07,000
Now, let's talk jackets.

156
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:09,000
I kinda like the first one.

157
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:12,700
No, that's a bit too
much Hell's Angel,
I think I like the shorter one.

158
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:15,900
Look, waist-length, nice
and slimming, shows off the bum.

159
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:20,500
Works for me. Once we've got an
outfit, we can look at the face.

160
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,500
Ever thought about cosmetic
surgery?

161
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:27,300
I've considered it. A little
lift around the eyes, tighten up
the jaw line. What do you think?

162
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:30,200
Oh, let's have
a bit more ambition!

163
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:33,500
Let's do something. . .cutting edge.

164
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:36,100
So, Rose, what do you actually do?

165
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:41,500
I just travel about a bit,
a bit of a. . .tourist, I suppose.

166
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:43,800
Another way of saying unemployed?
No.

167
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:47,500
Have you got a job?
Well, not really, no, but. . .

168
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:52,700
Then you ARE unemployed, and yet
you've still got enough money
to buy peroxide. Why Fitch?

169
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:59,500
I think she got a few of
the questions wrong, that's all.
And you'd know all about that.

170
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:05,100
Well, yeah, but I can't vote for
myself, so it had to be Fitch.

171
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:10,100
I'm sorry, that's the game,
that's how it works.

172
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:12,100
I had to vote for someone.

173
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:15,800
Let me try again, it was the lights
and everything, I couldn't think.

174
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:21,700
In fact, with three answers wrong,
Broff was the weakest link in that
round, but it's votes that count.

175
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:24,700
I'm sorry, please. . .

176
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,400
Oh, God, help me!

177
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,900
Fitch, you are the weakest link.
Goodbye.

178
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:45,100
And we've gone to the adverts,
back in three minutes!

179
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:47,900
What was that? What just happened?

180
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:50,900
She was the weakest link,
she gets disintegrated.

181
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,800
Blasted into atoms.

182
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:57,700
But I voted for her!

183
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,500
Oh, my God, this is sick!

184
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:06,500
All of you, you're just sick!
I'm not playing this!
I'm not playing!

185
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:11,200
I. . .I can't do it!

186
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:15,100
Oh, please, somebody let me out!

187
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:16,800
You are the weakest link.

188
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,200
Goodbye.

189
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:29,500
Don't try to escape.

190
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:32,800
It's play. . .or die.

191
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:41,400
Doctor,
they said all housemates must gather
on the sofa, you've got to.

192
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,100
I'm busy getting out, thanks.

193
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:46,800
But if you don't obey, then
all the housemates get punished.

194
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,900
Well, maybe I'll be voted out, then.

195
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,400
How stupid are you? You've only
just joined, you're not eligible.

196
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:55,000
Don't try anything clever
or we all get it in the neck.

197
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,100
Big Brother house,
this is Davina-droid.

198
00:12:58,100 --> 00:13:02,100
Crosbie, Lynda and Strood,
you have all been nominated
for eviction.

199
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:07,000
And the eighth person to be
evicted from the Big Brother house
is. . .

200
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:12,400
Crosbie!
Oh, I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

201
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:15,400
It should've been me,
that's not fair. Oh, Crosbie. . .

202
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:20,200
Crosbie, you have ten
seconds to make your farewells
and then we're gonna get you.

203
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,800
I won't forget you!
I'm sorry I stole your soap.

204
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,500
I don't mind, honestly!

205
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:29,400
Thanks for the food, you were
a smashing cook, bless you.

206
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:32,300
Crosbie, please leave
the Big Brother house.

207
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:40,300
Bye, then. Bye, Lynda.

208
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:41,800
Bye. . .

209
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:54,900
I don't believe it, poor Crosbie.

210
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:58,300
It's only a game show!
She'll make a fortune on the outside.

211
00:13:58,300 --> 00:14:03,000
Sell her story,
release a record, fitness video,
all of that, she'll be laughing.

212
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:06,600
What do you mean, on the outside?
Here we go.

213
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:19,900
Well, what are they waiting for?
Why don't they just let her go?
Stop it, it's not funny!

214
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:28,600
Eviction in five, four,
three, two, one!

215
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:38,500
What was that?

216
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:42,200
Disintegrator beam.

217
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,900
She's been evicted.

218
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:52,100
>From life.

219
00:14:58,900 --> 00:15:02,400
No-one programmed the transmat,
no-one selected the new contestants.

220
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:05,300
It is exactly like those stories.
Oh, don't start that again.

221
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:07,400
I think you need to
take a session off.

222
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:11,300
I would, if you'd take it with me.
And don't start that again either.

223
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:15,200
Though the rumours go back decades,
saying that something's been
hidden up here

224
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:17,800
underneath the transmissions.

225
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:19,900
But the controller would know.

226
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,300
She watches everything.

227
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:24,300
Maybe she just can't see it.

228
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:28,000
You've got to allow for human error.
Well, that's your problem, then.

229
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:32,800
I don't think she's been human
for years.

230
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:48,100
18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, transmit.

231
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:49,300
Are you insane?

232
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:54,300
You just step right into the
disintegrator? Is it that important,
getting your face on the telly?

233
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:56,800
Is it worth dying for? !
We haven't got a choice!

234
00:15:56,800 --> 00:16:00,900
But I thought you had to apply.
Don't be so stupid, that's how
they played it centuries back.

235
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,100
You get chosen whether
you like it or not.

236
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:07,600
Everyone on Earth is a potential
contestant, the transmat beam
picks you out at random.

237
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:10,700
It's non-stop, there are 60
Big Brother Houses running at once.

238
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:14,000
How many, 60?! They've had to
cut back, it's not what it was.

239
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:15,900
It's a charnel house!

240
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:20,900
What about the winners, what do they
get? They get to live. Is that it? !
Well, isn't that enough?

241
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:25,500
Rose is out there. She got caught
in the transmat, she's a contestant.

242
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:27,200
Time I got out.

243
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:31,800
That other contestant, Linda with an
I, she was forcibly evicted for what?

244
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:35,500
Damage to property. What, like this?

245
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:43,500
No, I'm just not getting this,
it's just too. . .safe, too decent.
And you'd never keep it clean.

246
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,300
Stage two ready and waiting.

247
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,400
Bring it on, girls.

248
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:55,200
Now it's time for the face-off!

249
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:57,500
Does that mean I get
to compete with someone else?

250
00:16:57,600 --> 00:17:01,000
No, like I said, face. . .off.

251
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:06,900
I think you'd look good
with a dog's head.

252
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:10,300
Or maybe no head at all,
that would be so outrageous.

253
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:13,300
And we could stitch your legs
to the middle of your chest.

254
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:16,100
Nothing is too extreme,
it's to die for!

255
00:17:16,100 --> 00:17:18,700
Now hold on, ladies, I don't want
to have to shoot either one of you.

256
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:20,500
But you're unarmed.
You're naked!

257
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:24,200
But that's a Compact Laser Deluxe!

258
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:26,300
Where were you hiding that?

259
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:30,000
You really don't want to know.
Give me that accessory!

260
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:36,300
You are the weakest link, goodbye!

261
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:45,400
Going to the break,
two minutes on the clock.

262
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:49,100
Just a reminder, we've got solar
flare activity coming up in ten.

263
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:52,500
Colleen was clever, she banked all
the money, why'd you you vote
for her?

264
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:54,100
Cos I want to keep you in!

265
00:17:54,100 --> 00:17:57,900
You're stupid, you don't even know
the Princess Vossaheen's surname.

266
00:17:57,900 --> 00:18:00,600
When it comes to the final,
I want to be up against you.

267
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:07,500
So that you get disintegrated and I
get a load of credits, courtesy of
the Bad Wolf Corporation.

268
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:09,900
What do you mean? Who's Bad Wolf?

269
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:14,000
They're in charge.
They run the Game Station.

270
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,600
Why are they called Bad Wolf?

271
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:17,600
I dunno, it's just a name.

272
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:20,700
It's like an old Earth
nursery rhyme, what does it matter?

273
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:25,100
I keep hearing those words
everywhere we go, Bad Wolf. . .

274
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:29,800
The things you've seen. . .
The darkness!

275
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:33,600
The big bad wolf.

276
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:37,400
Attention, all personnel, Bad Wolf
One descending. Blaidd Drwg. . .

277
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:40,000
What does it mean? Bad Wolf.

278
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:48,000
Different times, different places,
like it's written all over the
universe. What are you on about?

279
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:52,700
If the Bad Wolf are in charge
of the quiz, then. . .
maybe I'm not here by mistake.

280
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:57,400
Someone's been planning this.

281
00:18:57,400 --> 00:19:03,300
The Doctor, you've broken the
house rules, Big Brother has
no choice but to evict you.

282
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:08,500
You have ten seconds
to make your farewells,
and then we're gonna get you.

283
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:11,700
Come on, then, open up! You're mad,
it's like you want to die!

284
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:15,000
I reckon he's a plant, he was
only brought in to stir things up.

285
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,600
The Doctor, please
leave the Big Brother house.

286
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:22,000
Come on, then! Disintegrate me!

287
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:25,200
Come on, what are you waiting for?
He's mad, he's bonkers.

288
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:27,800
I told you to keep an eye on him,
not kill him.

289
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:30,700
He damaged the property,
it's an automatic process.

290
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:36,400
Eviction in five, four. . .

291
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:39,000
three, two. . .

292
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,100
one!

293
00:19:43,900 --> 00:19:47,300
Ha-ha, I knew it! Do you see?
Someone brought me into this game.

294
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:51,500
If they wanted me dead, they could've
transmatted me into a volcano.
What did you do? Nothing,

295
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:54,200
it's like. . .some sort of override.

296
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:56,700
Maybe the security
isn't as tight this end.

297
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:59,300
Are you following this?
I'm getting out!

298
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:05,600
Come with me.

299
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:09,100
We're not allowed!
Stay in there, you've got a 50/50
chance of disintegration.

300
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:12,000
Stay with me, I promise
I'll get you out alive, come on!

301
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,000
No, I can't. . .I can't.
Lynda, you're sweet.

302
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,600
>From what I've seen of your world,
do you think anybody votes for sweet?

303
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:33,200
Hold on. . .I've been here before.

304
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:35,100
This is Satellite Five.

305
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:43,100
No guards. That makes a change.

306
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:46,700
You'd think a big business like
Satellite Five
would be armed to the teeth.

307
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:50,200
No-one's called it Satellite Five in
ages. It's the Game Station now.

308
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:52,800
It hasn't been Satellite Five
in about 100 years.

309
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:56,400
100 years exactly.
It's the year 200100.

310
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,800
I was here before, Floor 139.

311
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:01,700
The satellite was broadcasting
news channels back then.

312
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:05,400
I had a bit of trouble upstairs,
nothing too serious.

313
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:08,200
Easy, gave 'em a hand,
home in time for tea.

314
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,900
100 years ago?

315
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:14,200
What, you were here 100 years ago?
Yep.

316
00:21:14,300 --> 00:21:16,300
You're looking good on it.

317
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:17,900
I moisturise.

318
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:21,700
Funny sort of readings.
All kinds of energy.

319
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:26,000
The place is humming. It's weird.
This goes way beyond
normal transmissions.

320
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:29,400
What would they need all
that power for? I don't know,

321
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:33,000
I think we're the first ever
contestants to get outside.

322
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:37,000
I had two friends with me,
they must've got caught in the
same transmat, where would they be?

323
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,800
They could have been allocated
anywhere, there's 100
different games.

324
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:44,100
Like what? Well,
there's ten floors of Big Brother,

325
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:46,500
there's a different house
behind each door,

326
00:21:46,500 --> 00:21:49,500
and beyond that there's all sorts of
shows, it's non-stop.

327
00:21:49,500 --> 00:21:52,000
There's, em. . .Call My Bluff
with real guns,

328
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,500
Countdown where you've got 30
seconds to stop the bomb going off.

329
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:58,900
Ground Force, which is a nasty one,
you get turned into compost.

330
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,200
Erm. . .Wipeout,

331
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:04,600
speaks for itself, oh, and
Stars In Their Eyes, literally,

332
00:22:04,700 --> 00:22:08,200
stars in their eyes -
if you don't sing, you get blinded.

333
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:10,000
And you watch this stuff?

334
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,500
Everyone does. How come you don't?

335
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:14,000
I never paid for my licence.

336
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:16,500
Oh, my God,
you get executed for that!

337
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:18,900
Let 'em try.

338
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:21,800
You keep saying things
that don't make sense.

339
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:23,700
Who are you, though, Doctor, really?

340
00:22:23,700 --> 00:22:25,300
It doesn't matter.

341
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:29,800
Well, it does to me.
I've just put my life in your hands.

342
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,400
I'm a traveller wandering past.

343
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:34,000
Believe it or not,
all I'm after is a quiet life.

344
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:39,000
So. . .if we get out of here,
what are you gonna do,
just. . .wander off again?

345
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:41,200
Fast as I can.

346
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:44,900
Cos, em. . .I could come with ya.

347
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:49,100
Maybe you could.

348
00:22:49,100 --> 00:22:52,000
I wouldn't get in the way.
I wouldn't mind if you did.

349
00:22:52,100 --> 00:22:55,500
Not a bad idea, Lynda with a Y.

350
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:59,200
But first of all we've gotta
concentrate on the getting out,

351
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:02,900
and to do that, you've got to know
your enemy. Who's controlling it?

352
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:06,100
Who's in charge of the satellite now?
Hold on. . .

353
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Your lords and masters.

354
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:23,200
OK, you win, the
Controller's got to handle this.

355
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:26,500
Archive makes a record of
all transmat activities.

356
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:28,900
Find out how he got on board.
Archive Six.

357
00:23:53,100 --> 00:23:54,900
Controller. . .

358
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:57,000
we have a problem.

359
00:23:57,100 --> 00:23:58,600
Continue working.

360
00:23:58,700 --> 00:24:00,600
We have a security problem.

361
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:02,400
Continue working.

362
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:09,900
I'm sorry, but I can't. We have
contestants outside the games,
but the alarms haven't gone off.

363
00:24:09,900 --> 00:24:12,500
No security, the games continue.

364
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:15,900
We can't just let them wander.
They are no-one.

365
00:24:17,900 --> 00:24:19,900
They are no-one.

366
00:24:24,900 --> 00:24:27,000
I'm sorry, I was just, erm. . .

367
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,900
Archive Six is out of bounds.

368
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:32,100
But I need to check the transmat log.
Archive Six is out of bounds.

369
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:34,300
No-one may enter Archive Six.

370
00:24:34,400 --> 00:24:36,000
Return to work.

371
00:24:41,500 --> 00:24:43,200
Return to work.

372
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:48,800
Inform all staff,
solar flares in delta point seven.

373
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:51,100
19, 20. . .

374
00:24:53,900 --> 00:24:56,400
Compatible systems. . .

375
00:24:56,500 --> 00:24:59,700
Just align the wave signature. . .

376
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:03,100
That-a-boy! Got myself a gun!

377
00:25:03,100 --> 00:25:08,100
Well, ladies, the pleasure was
all mine, which is the only
thing that matters in the end.

378
00:25:15,500 --> 00:25:17,400
Two hearts, that's him.

379
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:18,900
Which floor?

380
00:25:24,700 --> 00:25:26,900
Blimey!

381
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:30,300
I've never seen it for real before,
not from orbit.

382
00:25:30,300 --> 00:25:32,000
Planet Earth!

383
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:36,300
What's happened to it?
It's always been like that,
ever since I was born. See there?

384
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:39,000
That's
the Great Atlantic Smog Storm.

385
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:41,700
We get newsflashes, telling us
when it's safe to breathe outside.

386
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:43,700
So the population just sits there.

387
00:25:43,700 --> 00:25:46,800
Half the world's too fat, half's too
thin, and you lot just watch telly.

388
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:49,700
10, 000 channels,
all beaming down from here.

389
00:25:49,700 --> 00:25:53,500
The human race! Brainless sheep,
being fed on a diet of. . .

390
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:56,600
Mind you, have they still got
that programme where three
people live with a bear?

391
00:25:56,600 --> 00:26:00,700
Oh, Bear With Me, I love that one!
And me. The celebrity edition
where the bear got in the bath. . .

392
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:04,000
But it's all gone wrong,
I mean, history's gone wrong, again!

393
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:07,000
This should be the Fourth Great and
Bountiful Human Empire.

394
00:26:07,100 --> 00:26:10,300
I don't understand.
Last time I was here I put it right.

395
00:26:10,300 --> 00:26:13,800
No, but that's when it first went
wrong, 100 years ago, like you said.

396
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:16,800
All the news channels,
they just shut down overnight.

397
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,600
But that was me. I did that.

398
00:26:20,600 --> 00:26:24,600
There was nothing left in their
place, no information.
The whole planet froze.

399
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:29,300
The government, the economy, they
collapsed. That was the start of it,

400
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:31,000
100 years of hell.

401
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,500
Oh, my. . .

402
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:38,600
I made this world.

403
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:50,600
That leaves Rose and Rodrick,
you're going head-to-head.

404
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:53,500
Let's play. . .the Weakest Link!

405
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:55,500
That's the end of tactical voting.

406
00:26:55,600 --> 00:26:57,000
You're on your own now.

407
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:04,100
Hey, handsome, good to see you.
Any sign of Rose?
Can't you track her down?

408
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:06,900
She must be still inside the games,
all the rooms are shielded.

409
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:09,900
If I can get inside this computer.
She's got to be here somewhere.

410
00:27:09,900 --> 00:27:12,400
Hurry, these games
don't have a happy ending.

411
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:14,600
You think I don't know that? !

412
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:19,100
There you go. Patch that in,
it's programmed to find her.

413
00:27:19,100 --> 00:27:21,000
Thanks. Hey, there. Hello!

414
00:27:21,100 --> 00:27:23,200
Captain Jack Harkness. Lynda Moss.

415
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:25,600
Nice to meet you, Lynda Moss.
Do you mind flirting outside?

416
00:27:25,600 --> 00:27:27,700
I was just saying hello!
For you, that's flirting.

417
00:27:27,800 --> 00:27:29,600
I'm not complaining. Muchas gracias.

418
00:27:29,700 --> 00:27:33,300
Not compatible! This stupid
system doesn't make sense!

419
00:27:36,600 --> 00:27:41,100
This place should be a basic
broadcaster, but the systems
are twice as complicated.

420
00:27:41,100 --> 00:27:44,200
It's more than TV, this station's
transmitting something else.
Like what?

421
00:27:44,300 --> 00:27:47,700
I don't know. This whole
Bad Wolf thing's tied up with me.

422
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:52,100
Someone's manipulating my entire
life, it's some sort of trap,
and Rose is stuck inside it.

423
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:56,900
Rose, in geography,
the Grand Central Ravine is named
after which ancient British city?

424
00:27:57,900 --> 00:28:01,700
Is it York? No, the correct
answer is Sheffield.

425
00:28:01,800 --> 00:28:06,800
Found her! Floor 407. Oh, my God,
she's with the Anne-droid,
get her out of there!

426
00:28:06,800 --> 00:28:10,600
Rodrick, in literature, the
author of Lucky was Jackie who?

427
00:28:10,700 --> 00:28:15,400
Stewart.
No, the correct answer is Collins.

428
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:19,000
Rose, the oldest inhabitant
of the Isop Galaxy

429
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:22,000
is the face of what? Boe!
The Face of Boe!

430
00:28:24,900 --> 00:28:26,600
That is the correct answer.

431
00:28:30,100 --> 00:28:32,300
Come on! Come on!

432
00:28:32,300 --> 00:28:36,800
Rodrick, in history who was the
president of the Red Velvets?

433
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:38,700
Hoshbin Frane.

434
00:28:38,700 --> 00:28:40,100
That is correct.

435
00:28:40,100 --> 00:28:46,000
Rose, food, the dish gaffabeque
originated on which planet?

436
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Em. . .is it. . . ?

437
00:28:53,900 --> 00:28:55,400
Mars?

438
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:58,700
No, the correct answer is Lucifer.

439
00:29:03,500 --> 00:29:08,100
Rodrick, which measurement
of length is said
to have been defined

440
00:29:08,100 --> 00:29:09,500
by the Emperor Jate

441
00:29:09,600 --> 00:29:12,200
as the distance from his nose
to his fingertip?

442
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:17,600
Would that be a goffle?
No, the correct answer is a paab.

443
00:29:17,700 --> 00:29:21,800
Rose, in fashion, Stella Pok Baint
is famous for what?

444
00:29:26,100 --> 00:29:27,900
Shoes.

445
00:29:27,900 --> 00:29:30,200
No. The correct answer is hats.
Rodrick. . .

446
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:34,100
Game Room Six, which one is it?
Over here!

447
00:29:34,100 --> 00:29:36,700
San Hazeldine.

448
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:38,800
No, the correct answer
is San Chen.

449
00:29:38,800 --> 00:29:41,800
Let me blast it open.
You can't, it's a vital combination.

450
00:29:41,900 --> 00:29:48,500
Rose, in history, which Icelandic
city hosted Murder Spree 20?

451
00:29:54,700 --> 00:29:56,800
Reykjavik?

452
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:03,300
No, the correct answer
is Pola Ventura.

453
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:10,600
Oh, my God! I've done it!
You've lost!

454
00:30:12,200 --> 00:30:14,900
Cone on, come on, come on!

455
00:30:14,900 --> 00:30:18,100
Rodrick. . . I'm not mean to be
here. . .you ARE the strongest
link.

456
00:30:18,200 --> 00:30:21,300
I need to find the Doctor,
he's gotta be here somewhere!

457
00:30:21,300 --> 00:30:24,200
He wouldn't just leave me!

458
00:30:24,300 --> 00:30:27,700
Thank you so much. This game is
illegal, I'm telling you to stop!

459
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:31,100
Rose! Stop this game!
I order you to stop this game!

460
00:30:31,100 --> 00:30:32,600
You are the weakest link. . . .

461
00:30:32,600 --> 00:30:35,200
Look out for the Anne-droid,
it's armed!

462
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:41,800
What the hell did you do to her?

463
00:30:41,800 --> 00:30:45,200
I'm calling security,
you have no permission to be here.

464
00:30:45,300 --> 00:30:46,900
Deactivate the Anne-droid.

465
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:51,500
You killed her and all
you're worried about money? !
Back off, mister! Back off!

466
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:56,100
Control, I'm overriding your
commands, I need security,
and I need it here right now!

467
00:30:56,100 --> 00:30:57,700
It's that lot. . .

468
00:30:57,800 --> 00:30:59,500
Leave him alone!

469
00:30:59,500 --> 00:31:02,400
Sir, put down the gun
or I'll have to shoot.

470
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:07,600
You killed her! Your stupid
freaking game show killed her!

471
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:12,600
Sir, I'm arresting you under Private
Legislation 16 of the Game Station
Syndicate. . .

472
00:31:28,100 --> 00:31:30,900
Can you tell us the
purpose of this device, sir?

473
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,300
Can you tell us how you got
on board?

474
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:35,800
Just leave him alone.

475
00:31:35,900 --> 00:31:37,700
I'm asking him.

476
00:31:40,700 --> 00:31:43,400
Sir? Can you tell us who you are?

477
00:31:49,500 --> 00:31:54,000
You will be taken from this
place to the lunar penal colony,
to be held without trial.

478
00:31:54,100 --> 00:31:56,700
You may not appeal
against this sentence.

479
00:31:58,400 --> 00:32:00,800
Is that understood?

480
00:32:06,700 --> 00:32:08,300
Let's do it.

481
00:32:20,600 --> 00:32:22,700
Oh, my God, now we're in trouble.

482
00:32:24,200 --> 00:32:26,400
Floor 500.

483
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:28,900
Clear the floor!

484
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:31,500
He's on his way up here. . .
with a gun!

485
00:32:36,500 --> 00:32:38,500
This is an emergency,
close down the lift.

486
00:32:38,600 --> 00:32:40,600
All staff are reminded that
solar flares commence. . .

487
00:32:40,700 --> 00:32:43,300
Never mind solar flares,
he's gonna kill you!

488
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:49,700
OK, move away from the desk.
Nobody try anything clever.

489
00:32:49,800 --> 00:32:53,700
Everybody clear, stand to the side
and stay there.

490
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:55,600
Who's in charge of this place?
19, 20. . .

491
00:32:55,700 --> 00:32:59,700
This satellite's more than
a game station. 79, 80. . .
Who killed Rose Tyler?

492
00:32:59,800 --> 00:33:02,800
All staff are reminded. . .
I want an answer!

493
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:04,600
She can't reply. Don't shoot!

494
00:33:04,700 --> 00:33:07,000
Oh, don't be so thick,
like I was ever gonna shoot.

495
00:33:07,100 --> 00:33:11,500
Captain, we've got more guards on the
way up, secure the exits. Yes, sir!
What were you saying?

496
00:33:11,500 --> 00:33:17,000
But. . .I've got your gun. OK, so
shoot me. Why can't she answer?
She's, erm. . . Can I put this down?

497
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:19,600
If you want, just hurry up. Thanks.

498
00:33:19,700 --> 00:33:21,300
Sorry, erm. . .

499
00:33:21,300 --> 00:33:24,900
The Controller is linked into
the transmissions, the entire
output goes through her brain.

500
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:28,700
You're not a member of staff, so she
doesn't recognise your existence.
What's her name?

501
00:33:28,800 --> 00:33:33,800
I don't know. She was installed
when she was five years old, that's
the only life she's ever known.

502
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:36,300
Doors sealed, we're safe for about
ten minutes. Keep an eye on 'em.

503
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:39,400
That stuff about something going on
with the Game Station,
I think you're right.

504
00:33:39,500 --> 00:33:43,400
I've kept a log, unauthorised
transmats, encrypted signals.

505
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:45,200
It's been going on for years.
Show me.

506
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:48,100
You're not allowed in there,
Archive Six is out of bounds.

507
00:33:48,100 --> 00:33:50,800
Do I look like an
out-of-bounds sort of guy?

508
00:34:17,300 --> 00:34:18,900
What the hell. . . ?

509
00:34:22,800 --> 00:34:24,500
Solar flare activity in delta. . .

510
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:28,400
If you're not holding us hostage,
let us out, the staff are terrified!

511
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:32,400
That's the same staff who
execute hundreds of contestants?
We're just doing our jobs.

512
00:34:32,500 --> 00:34:36,400
With that sentence you
just lost the right to even
talk to me, now back off!

513
00:34:40,300 --> 00:34:41,900
That's just the solar flares.

514
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:46,500
They interfere with the
broadcast signal, so this place
automatically powers down.

515
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:51,100
Planet Earth gets a few repeats.
It's all quite normal. Doctor. . .

516
00:34:51,100 --> 00:34:55,300
Doctor? Whatever it is,
you can wait. I think she wants you.

517
00:34:55,300 --> 00:34:58,200
Doctor. . . Doctor. . .

518
00:34:58,300 --> 00:35:00,600
Where's the Doctor? I'm here.

519
00:35:00,700 --> 00:35:03,500
I can't see, blind. . .

520
00:35:03,600 --> 00:35:05,600
So blind, all my life blind.

521
00:35:05,700 --> 00:35:09,000
All I can see is numbers,
but I saw you. What do you want?

522
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:11,300
Solar flares hiding me,
they can't hear me.

523
00:35:11,300 --> 00:35:13,800
My masters listen, but they can't
hear me now, the sun,

524
00:35:13,800 --> 00:35:16,500
the sun is so bright.
Who are your masters?

525
00:35:16,600 --> 00:35:18,900
They wired my head,
the name is forbidden.

526
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:22,000
They control my thoughts,

527
00:35:22,100 --> 00:35:26,100
my masters, I had to be careful.
They monitor transmission.
but they don't watch the programmes.

528
00:35:26,200 --> 00:35:30,000
I could hide you inside the games.
My friend died inside your games.

529
00:35:30,100 --> 00:35:32,600
It doesn't matter.
Don't you dare tell me that!

530
00:35:32,600 --> 00:35:38,100
They've been hiding, my masters,
hiding in the dark space,
watching and shaping the Earth,

531
00:35:38,100 --> 00:35:40,500
so. . .so. . .so many years.

532
00:35:40,500 --> 00:35:45,200
Always been there, guiding humanity,
hundreds and hundreds of years.

533
00:35:45,200 --> 00:35:48,100
Who are they? They wait and plan
and grow in numbers,

534
00:35:48,100 --> 00:35:51,200
they're strong now,
so strong, my masters. Who are they?

535
00:35:51,300 --> 00:35:53,100
But speak of you.

536
00:35:53,200 --> 00:35:57,000
My masters, they fear the Doctor.
Tell me! Who are they?

537
00:36:03,100 --> 00:36:05,900
When's the next solar flare?
Two years' time.

538
00:36:05,900 --> 00:36:08,300
Fat lot of good that is!
Found the Tardis.

539
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:11,500
We're not leaving now.
No, but the Tardis worked it out.

540
00:36:11,500 --> 00:36:15,400
You'll wanna watch this.
Lynda, could you stand
over there for me, please?

541
00:36:15,500 --> 00:36:17,100
I just wanna go home.

542
00:36:17,100 --> 00:36:21,000
It'll only take a second,
could you stand in that spot?
Quick as you can!

543
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:22,600
Everybody watching?

544
00:36:22,600 --> 00:36:26,000
OK, three, two, one.

545
00:36:30,500 --> 00:36:33,700
But you killed her! Oh, do you think?

546
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:44,400
What the hell was that? It's a
transmat beam, not a disintegrator,
a secondary transmat system.

547
00:36:44,500 --> 00:36:48,600
People don't get killed in the
games, they get transported
across Space.

548
00:36:48,700 --> 00:36:51,700
Doctor, Rose is still alive!

549
00:37:03,600 --> 00:37:05,700
No, it can't be.

550
00:37:08,600 --> 00:37:10,100
I saw you die!

551
00:37:14,400 --> 00:37:16,300
She's out there somewhere! Doctor!

552
00:37:16,300 --> 00:37:18,400
Coordinates 5.6.1.

553
00:37:18,500 --> 00:37:21,300
Don't, the solar flare's gone,
they'll hear you!

554
00:37:21,400 --> 00:37:23,500
No, my masters, no, I defy you!

555
00:37:23,600 --> 00:37:29,500
Sigma 7. . . A-a-a-ah! They took her.

556
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,600
Oh, my masters. . .

557
00:37:52,100 --> 00:37:54,600
you can kill me. . .

558
00:37:54,600 --> 00:37:56,900
for I have brought your destruction.

559
00:38:02,600 --> 00:38:05,300
Look, use that. It might contain
the final numbers,

560
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:09,500
I kept a log of all the unscheduled
transmissions. Nice. . .Thanks.

561
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:11,700
Captain Jack Harkness, by the way.

562
00:38:11,700 --> 00:38:14,500
I'm Davitch Pavale.
Nice to meet you, Davitch Pavale.

563
00:38:14,600 --> 00:38:16,000
There's a time and a place.

564
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:19,400
Are you saying that this whole
set-up's been a disguise all along?

565
00:38:19,500 --> 00:38:22,600
Going way back, installing the
Jagrafess 100 years ago.

566
00:38:22,600 --> 00:38:28,100
Someone's been playing a long game,
controlling the human race from
behind the scenes for generations.

567
00:38:28,200 --> 00:38:29,600
Click on this.

568
00:38:33,100 --> 00:38:35,200
The transmat delivers to that point,

569
00:38:35,200 --> 00:38:38,500
right on the edge of the solar
system. But there's nothing there.

570
00:38:38,600 --> 00:38:41,700
It looks like nothing because that's
what this satellite does.

571
00:38:41,700 --> 00:38:45,100
Underneath the transmission
there's another signal. Doing what?

572
00:38:45,200 --> 00:38:47,100
Hiding whatever's out there.

573
00:38:47,200 --> 00:38:49,600
Hiding it from sonar, radar, scanner.

574
00:38:49,700 --> 00:38:54,400
There's something's sitting
right on top of Planet Earth,
but it's completely invisible.

575
00:38:55,400 --> 00:38:57,300
If I cancel the signal. . .

576
00:39:14,600 --> 00:39:16,900
That's impossible.

577
00:39:16,900 --> 00:39:20,100
I know those ships.
They were destroyed.

578
00:39:21,600 --> 00:39:24,300
Obviously, they survived.
Who did? Who are they?

579
00:39:24,300 --> 00:39:26,300
200 ships.

580
00:39:26,300 --> 00:39:29,400
More than 2, 000 on board each one.

581
00:39:29,500 --> 00:39:31,400
That's just about
half a million of them.

582
00:39:31,500 --> 00:39:33,100
Half a million what?

583
00:39:33,100 --> 00:39:34,900
Daleks.

584
00:39:34,900 --> 00:39:38,900
Alert! Alert! We are detected!

585
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:42,000
It is the Doctor!
He has located us!

586
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:44,500
Open communications channel!

587
00:39:44,500 --> 00:39:49,700
The female will stand! Stand!

588
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:58,300
I will talk to the Doctor.

589
00:39:58,300 --> 00:40:01,000
Oh, will you? That's nice, hello!

590
00:40:01,100 --> 00:40:03,500
The Dalek stratagem
nears completion.

591
00:40:03,500 --> 00:40:07,500
The fleet is almost ready.
You will not intervene.

592
00:40:07,500 --> 00:40:09,500
Oh, really? Why's that, then?

593
00:40:09,600 --> 00:40:12,200
We have your associate.

594
00:40:12,300 --> 00:40:17,400
You will obey or she
will be exterminated.

595
00:40:18,400 --> 00:40:19,900
No.

596
00:40:26,300 --> 00:40:27,800
Explain yourself.

597
00:40:27,900 --> 00:40:30,100
I said "no".

598
00:40:30,100 --> 00:40:32,800
What is the meaning
of this negative?

599
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:36,300
It means no.
But she will be destroyed!

600
00:40:36,300 --> 00:40:40,000
No. . .cos this is what I'M gonna do.

601
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:44,000
I'm gonna rescue her, I'm gonna save
Rose Tyler from the middle of the
Dalek fleet,

602
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:47,500
and then I'm gonna save the Earth,
and then just to finish off,

603
00:40:47,600 --> 00:40:51,600
I'm gonna wipe every last
stinking Dalek out of the sky!

604
00:40:51,700 --> 00:40:56,000
But you have no weapons,
no defences, no plan!

605
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:57,700
Yeah. . .

606
00:40:57,700 --> 00:41:00,500
and doesn't that scare you to death?

607
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:02,500
Rose? Yes, Doctor?

608
00:41:02,600 --> 00:41:05,400
I'm coming to get you.

609
00:41:05,400 --> 00:41:10,900
The Doctor is initiating hostile action!
The statagem must advance!

610
00:41:10,900 --> 00:41:13,900
Begin the invasion of Earth!

611
00:41:13,900 --> 00:41:16,300
The Doctor will be exterminated!

612
00:41:16,400 --> 00:41:17,900
Exterminate! Exterminate!

613
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:19,900
Exterminate!

614
00:41:19,900 --> 00:41:24,500
Exterminate! Exterminate!

615
00:41:28,200 --> 00:41:31,600
Launch missiles, exterminate.

616
00:41:31,600 --> 00:41:36,200
We've got incoming! This is it,
ladies and gentlemen, we are at war.

617
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:39,400
There's an army
about to invade this station.

618
00:41:40,300 --> 00:41:41,600
Defences have gone off-line.

619
00:41:41,700 --> 00:41:42,400
I'm dead or about to die any
second with no chance of escape.

620
00:41:44,500 --> 00:41:45,700
I'm dead or about to die any
second with no chance of escape.

621
00:41:51,400 --> 00:41:52,800
They interfere with the
broadcast signal, so this place
automatically powers down.

622
00:41:57,900 --> 00:42:00,800
How did you survive the Time War?

623
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:03,800
They survived through me!

624
00:42:16,600 --> 00:42:23,700
